  "sample": {
    "description": "Daily OHLCV for SPY, QQQ, DIA from Yahoo Finance via market_data.get_prices; full history from first available trading day through last test trading day; training and testing intervals follow paper definition (training up to end of 2022, testing from start of 2023 through end of Feb 2026 window); ETFs as index proxies",
    "n": 2050,
    "start": "2018-01-02",
    "end": "2026-02-27",
    "same_as_paper": true,
    "missing": 0,
    "extra": 0,
    "differences": "",
    "cannot_count": "",
    "not_rebuilt": {},
    "substitutions": "ETFs SPY/QQQ/DIA as proxies for S&P 500/NASDAQ-100/DJIA indices; Yahoo Finance vendor; next-day open execution; integer shares with floor(cash/(open*(1+cost))); sigma_i interpreted as (High-Low)/Close because STD of single High-Low undefined without extra window; P* window N chosen as standard trading month (paper leaves N unstated); EMA via pandas ewm adjust=False span; Sharpe sqrt(252); MDD as max peak-to-trough; HAC Newey-West lags=5 Bartlett; block bootstrap length 5 with 1000 resamples"
  },
  "notes": "Choices the paper leaves open: (1) Paper defines P*_t with sum over i=t-N to t-1 but never states N; we chose N as standard trading month consistent with MA reference in text; other N values produce very different VP-MACD trade counts. (2) sigma_i = STD(High-Low)/Close: STD of single daily High-Low is undefined; we implemented sigma_i=(High-Low)/Close (range-based normalized volatility) which is the only literal implementable reading without an extra undocumented rolling window; alternative rolling STD over N or other window shifts trade counts and PnL. (3) r_i uses absolute body ratio |Close-Open|/(High-Low) as stated. (4) Data source: paper uses Yahoo Finance Close; we use close field from yfinance (unadjusted close) for signal generation; open for execution is unadjusted. (5) EMA initialization: alpha=2/(n+1) with recursive EMA_t = alpha*P_t+(1-alpha)*EMA_{t-1} initialized via pandas ewm adjust=False min_periods=n. (6) Execution: paper states next trading day open to avoid look-ahead bias; we implement signal at close of t executed at open of t+1; if signal on last test day no execution possible. (7) Position handling: long-only, fully invested, floor to integer shares, cost one-way applied as price*(1+cost) at entry and price*(1-cost) at exit equivalent to cost per share; paper states one-way cost and round-trip, we apply at both entry and exit. (8) Metrics: total PnL = V_T - V_0 where V_0 is initial capital at test start and V_T mark-to-market including unrealized position at last close; win ratio = N_win/N completed buy-sell pairs (incomplete open position not counted); PnL ratio = avgGain/avgLoss in USD; expectancy = winRatio*avgGain - (1-winRatio)*avgLoss; Sharpe = mean(R)/sd(R)*sqrt(252) where R_t = (V_t - V_{t-1})/V_{t-1} (daily portfolio returns, zero when flat); MDD as max(Peak - Value)/Peak. (9) Statistical tests: one-sided t-test on daily return differences with t_{T-1} p-values; Newey-West HAC t with Bartlett weights lags=5 (paper does not state bandwidth) and normal p-values; circular block bootstrap with block length 5, B as stated, p = proportion of bootstrap mean differences <=0 (one-sided). (10) Deviations: Our baseline and MACD+lambda trade counts and PnLs differ from paper likely due to Yahoo Finance data vintage differences, dividend/split adjustments, exact EMA warmup handling, and transaction cost application details; VP-MACD differences larger due to ambiguous N and sigma window as above; we report honest replication values without tuning N to match paper. Sample counts are derived purely from date range definition without trimming to paper counts."
}